Below is a minimal fix for the one vulnerable spot in report-generator.js. The problem is that in

  .replace(/%%LIGHTHOUSE_JAVASCRIPT%%/, sanitizedJavascript)

any dollar‐signs (`$`) inside your injected JS will be interpreted as replacement‐tokens (e.g. `$'`, `$&`, etc.). To avoid that, we must double every `$` in the string we pass to `.replace()`. One way is to post‐process `REPORT_JAVASCRIPT` with `.replace(/\$/g, '$$$$')`, which converts each single `$` into the string `$$` (so that when the outer `.replace()` runs, each `$$` becomes a single literal `$`).

