Explanation of the fix:

1. We locate the lone `generateReportHtml` method in  
   `lighthouse-core/report/v2/report-generator.js`.
2. After the existing “sanitize the `</` sequence” step, we chain on  
   `.replace(/\$/g, '$$$$')`.
3. In the inner `.replace(/\$/g, '$$$$')`, each real `$` in your renderer JS becomes the literal `$$` in the intermediate string.  
4. When that intermediate string is later substituted into the template by  
   `.replace(/%%LIGHTHOUSE_JAVASCRIPT%%/, sanitizedJavascript)`, the `$$` sequences turn back into single `$` characters—yet no single `$` ever survives unescaped into the replacement‐token parser.  

With this in place, any `$…` sequences in your injected JS are rendered literally, and you no longer accidentally invoke `$'` or other special replacement syntax.
